ctionEntry id="f3f06746-86b4-5991-8251-9f38cc12b22c" name="Veteran" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade"><constraints><constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" type="max" id="81dc6776-aafc-5cd1-a9f5-66dbcd42c8ea" /></constraints></selectionEntry></selectionEntries></selectionEntryGroup></selectionEntryGroups><costs><cost name="pts" typeId="b0e5f7a2-33c8-46ce-8f8f-148d8171da43" value="0.0" /></costs><selectionEntries><selectionEntry id="b3a13e48-16b1-5cf3-af58-7ee13c63600c" name="Vehicle" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="model"><constraints><constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" type="min" id="d719154a-44f2-57bc-b4c7-adc71d925ca7" /><constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" type="max" id="ce9ff95a-304c-52cd-bc1d-c2cb9c95621f" /></constraints></selectionEntry></selectionEntries></selectionEntry></selectionEntries>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="5c0a904b-5464-5f3e-ac80-f4ce4d026d94" name="Data set notes" hidden="false">
      <description>Built only from Armies of the Colonial Legion Alpha 0.1. The source itself is a WIP and includes placeholders, missing entries, typos, and incomplete selector details. Where an option has a per-model price, it is represented as a repeatable upgrade and the user must select the correct number to match the models affected. No missing rulebook content has been invented.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule id="5df80837-b97c-577c-854c-42aedfa3d4f1" name="Close Air Support" hidden="false">
      <description>A Colonial Forward Air Observer may call an Air Strike twice per game. Resolve the first normally; after it is resolved the observer may call the second. Rookie pilot results on the Air Strike chart may be re-rolled.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d80f7163-bd80-59a8-812c-8799caacde70" name="March of the Legion" hidden="false">
      <description>The Colonial Argenti r.II is treated as a carbine. Almost all Colonial infantry squads use carbines as their base weapon, and this is a free upgrade.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1f12d274-3e9b-5703-9c3f-aed26bda3012" name="Faith in Armour" hidden="false">
      <description>Colonial infantry and artillery within 6 inches of, or being transported or towed by, a friendly vehicle with Damage Value 8+ gain +1 morale. This does not stack from multiple vehicles, but can stack with similar bonuses. Whenever a friendly Colonial DV 8+ vehicle is destroyed, friendly infantry and artillery within 6 inches must take a morale test; on a failure they suffer 1 pin.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="0d425d94-4ba4-5043-b8ff-c6537235f27c" name="Meticulous Assault (Great War Era)" hidden="false">
      <description>Great War Era only. Colonial units ignore the -1 morale penalty on order tests to enter from reserve. Units that outflank may deploy 12 inches farther along their table edge than normal.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c7d5b524-3f4c-535e-bb17-d1142cb4e8f8" name="Inspiring Courage (Modern Era)" hidden="false">
      <description>Modern Era only. When a Green Colonial unit is upgraded from Inexperienced to Regular after taking a casualty, it gives +1 morale to Inexperienced Green units within 12 inches. This bonus does not stack. A Green unit within 12 inches of a previously upgraded unit becomes Regular on a 4, 5, or 6 when checking for its Green upgrade.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f4caef54-c162-5ec7-8096-19aae8e3a640" name="Armoured Platoon" hidden="false">
      <description>Custom Armoured Platoon selector for this data set. Choose exactly one Armoured Platoon Commander using the normal Colonial officer ranks and experience levels. That commander may attach one matching-experience Tank / SPG as the command vehicle. The command vehicle counts toward the platoon total. The platoon requires at least one Infantry Squad and a total of three to six Tank / SPG selections.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="4b8d8320-67c1-5d0b-9256-1fca58afdefc" name="Green" hidden="false"><description>Green inexperienced troops can improve their experience after first taking casualties, following the Bolt Action Third Edition Green rule.</description></rule><rule id="23936248-a396-5c1d-8510-19e9be27e7f0" name="Tank Hunters" hidden="false"><description>This unit has the Tank Hunters special rule while sticky grenades or Ignifists are selected.</description></rule><rule id="bee51587-542a-58fa-a349-8b72e3b81907" name="Stubborn" hidden="false"><description>Disciplined troops ignore pin marker penalties during the applicable morale tests.</description></rule><rule id="b0b138cd-8a5b-56fc-b092-d75b545918e4" name="Lead by example" hidden="false"><description>Friendly “green” units within 6” of this unit receive a +1 bonus to their morale if this unit has not failed an order test or morale test this round.</description></rule><rule id="8280fdf9-fd71-5df1-9eae-a2beb4f3d80d" name="Fanatics" hidden="false"><description>Fanatical troops are exceptionally difficult to break in close combat and follow the Bolt Action Third Edition Fanatics rules.</description></rule><rule id="91423626-d0dc-5335-ad59-b1e903948a45" name="Stubborn (if Fanatics not taken)" hidden="false"><description>Stubborn troops use their unmodified morale value when taking morale tests caused by casualties, as defined by Bolt Action Third Edition.</description></rule><rule id="e1182a09-4f64-59f6-b113-c58330b24749" name="Motorbikes" hidden="false"><description>If taken, a mounted squad uses the motorbikes rules (see main rulebook).</description></rule><rule id="1f76a30a-1b7d-5c5d-9c7f-5fd3b4d10713" name="Behind enemy lines" hidden="false"><description>When outflanking as described on page 119 of the main Bolt Action rulebook, partisans of all veterancies ignore the -1 modifier to the order test for coming onto the table.</description></rule><rule id="79aff6e0-dd47-56bc-9680-abd397a9ce04" name="Inexperienced partisans are Green" hidden="false"><description>Inexperienced partisans (rebels) have the Green special rule.</description></rule><rule id="ebc8e90c-ba6b-5f27-bddc-816cf21db240" name="Veteran partisans are Stubborn" hidden="false"><description>Veteran partisans (commandos) have the Stubborn special rule.</description></rule><rule id="4692d0dc-8dfd-51b0-bbc1-ccef88862358" name="Fixed" hidden="false"><description>A Fixed weapon is restricted in how it can move and fire; use the Bolt Action Third Edition Fixed weapon rules.</description></rule><rule id="092c24f4-6309-578a-aff6-91a845a96ec7" name="Shaped charge" hidden="false"><description>Shaped Charge weapons use their special armour-penetration behaviour against armoured targets as defined in Bolt Action Third Edition.</description></rule><rule id="4a256bca-95bc-52d9-976e-5c8e6be1348e" name="Bane long-range accuracy" hidden="false"><description>This weapon does not suffer the -1 “to hit” penalty when shooting at targets at over half range.</description></rule><rule id="30760721-3f7f-574c-b65b-5e48627cb480" name="Gast loader" hidden="false"><description>If a Gast is taken, one soldier must use a pistol to act as its loader.</description></rule><rule id="29cbd927-7dfd-5ecf-9f68-b5a4cfc58e28" name="Sniper" hidden="false"><description>Sniper scope range is 12” to 36”. Shots under 12” cannot use the scope and fire as a normal rifle.

To Hit: Receive a +1 modifier to hit when using the special sniper ability.
Cover: Snipers ignore cover modifiers completely.
Casualty Selection: If a sniper scores a hit and damage using the scope, the attacking player chooses the team leader (or specific model depending on the exact ruling context) as the casualty.
Orders: A Fire or Ambush order is required to use the scope; the scope cannot be used with an Advance order.</description></rule></sharedRules>
</catalogue>